{"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"symbolKind":"class","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RWLock"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RWLock"}],"roleHeading":"Class","title":"RWLock","externalID":"s:4GLib6RWLockC"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The GRWLock struct is an opaque data structure to represent a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reader-writer lock. It is similar to a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in that it allows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"multiple threads to coordinate access to a shared resource.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RWLock","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/rwlock"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RWLockProtocol"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"RWLock","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The difference to a mutex is that a reader-writer lock discriminates","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between read-only (‘reader’) and full (‘writer’) access. While only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"one thread at a time is allowed write access (by holding the ‘writer’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lock via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_rw_lock_writer_lock()"},{"type":"text","text":"), multiple threads can gain"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simultaneous read-only access (by holding the ‘reader’ lock via","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"g_rw_lock_reader_lock()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is unspecified whether readers or writers have priority in acquiring the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"lock when a reader already holds the lock and a writer is queued to acquire"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here is an example for an array with access functions:","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(C Language Example):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"C","code":["  GRWLock lock;","  GPtrArray *array;","","  gpointer","  my_array_get (guint index)","  {","    gpointer retval = NULL;","","    if (!array)","      return NULL;","","    g_rw_lock_reader_lock (&lock);","    if (index < array->len)","      retval = g_ptr_array_index (array, index);","    g_rw_lock_reader_unlock (&lock);","","    return retval;","  }","","  void","  my_array_set (guint index, gpointer data)","  {","    g_rw_lock_writer_lock (&lock);","","    if (!array)","      array = g_ptr_array_new ();","","    if (index >= array->len)","      g_ptr_array_set_size (array, index+1);","    g_ptr_array_index (array, index) = data;","","    g_rw_lock_writer_unlock (&lock);","  }"," "]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This example shows an array which can be accessed by many readers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(the "},{"code":"my_array_get()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function) simultaneously, whereas the writers"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(the "},{"code":"my_array_set()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function) will only be allowed one at a time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and only if no readers currently access the array. This is because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the potentially dangerous resizing of the array. Using these"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"functions is fully multi-thread safe now."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RWLock"},{"text":" is allocated in static storage then it can be used","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without initialisation.  Otherwise, you should call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"g_rw_lock_init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on it and ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_rw_lock_clear()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when done."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A GRWLock should only be accessed with the g_rw_lock_ functions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RWLock","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" type acts as an owner of an underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRWLock"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"It provides the methods that can operate on this data type through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RWLockProtocol","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RWLock","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a strong reference or owner of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRWLock"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifie